# Context

## Background
PR #106 introduced entity_tag and fixed the single-shot PUT and presigned
GET conditional sites, but three sites from PR #59 kept sending the bare
unquoted token: conditional DELETE, and CompleteMultipartUpload If-Match
in compose and multipart_put.

## Why This Way
S3 versions are stored unquoted (quotes trimmed on every read), so the
wire form must be rebuilt on every conditional request. entity_tag quotes
once and is idempotent for an already-quoted value, so it is safe for all
callers.

## Gotchas
- Do NOT port this fix to azure.rs: it stores versions in the quoted wire
  form already (version_of keeps the ETag as the service sent it), so its
  etag() pass-through helper is correct and quoting again would double-
  quote. azure/tests.rs pins the quoted form.
- gcs.rs needs no counterpart: conditions ride on numeric generations
  (parse_generation -> i64), not entity-tags.
- The tests module condition fakes hold the quoted wire form; reverting
  any production site to the bare token fails three named tests.

